  "sgg_form_id": "sf424",
  "description": "The standard cover page form used for most federal grant applications. Collects applicant organization information, project details, estimated funding, and authorized representative certification.",
  "notes": [
    "The draft groups application metadata, applicant organization and contact, opportunity, project, funding and the signing role separately. The contact does not ask for an address. Department and division retain the 30-character source limit.",
    "Eight opportunity or organization values are pre-populated. Date Received, signature and signing date belong to submission. The funding total is read-only, and its existing six-input SGG calculation needs integration support before installation.",
    "Four attachment purposes remain distinct. The older XML transform format cannot write the three nested single attachments. The structured mapping records their source elements for integration.",
    "The ordered applicant-type list represents the three DAT and XML source slots. The definition preserves existing SGG choice values. Named-slot mapping and the existing per-item H-label normalization need integration support.",
    "The State/Province choice uses the common address. Regular SGG enforces ZIP+4 for US addresses; the shared question does not. The source and integration owners need to agree on the boundary.",
    "The State Review choices use the original XSD casing. Existing SGG lowercases state in two saved strings and normalizes them during XML generation."
  ],
  "risks": [
    "The definition preserves existing monetary strings. The XSD requires nonnegative decimals and allows a larger total than the existing API string limit.",
    "Confirm affirmative certification, duplicate applicant types and strict date order against the existing SGG behavior before migration. The current definition uses the shared not-before rule, which allows equal dates."
  ],
